Short:        Identify hardware and more
Author:       Richard 'Shred' Koerber
Uploader:     aminet@shredzone.de (Richard Koerber)
Type:         util/libs
Version:      45.0
Requires:     AmigaOS 2.0 or higher
Architecture: m68k-amigaos >= 2.0.4

License:      GNU Lesser General Public License v3
Source:       https://codefloe.com/shred/identify
Website:      https://identify.shredzone.org

Identify is a system shared library that identifies your hardware
expansions, system parameters, and other IDs.

Features:

  - Identifies expansion card names, alerts, and function call names
  - Gives information about your Amiga model, CPU, OS version,
    available memory, chipset, and much more...
  - Supports from AmigaOS 2.0 up to the latest AmigaOS 3.2.3
  - The expansion database contains 369 manufacturers and 747 boards
  - Distinguishes between most GVP and Phase5 boards with unique ID
  - Tries to give at least a hint if the board name is not known yet
  - Also detects PCI boards (requires IdentifyPci packet!)
  - Fully FPGA, DraCo, and PowerPC compatible
  - Supports PowerUp and WarpOS
  - Fully localized (catalogs included: Deutsch, Français, Italiano)
  - Use the features in ARexx, with the included rexxidentify.library
  - English and German documentation

New in this release:

  - PCI board detection (requires openpci and IdentifyPci)
  - Detects new AmiGUS audio board
  - ListExp now hides virtual expansions (unless VIRTUAL option is
    given)
  - New IDTAG_EmptyIfUnknown tag to get empty strings for unknown
    manufacturers or boards.
  - Minor fixes in the include files

Identify is Open Source Software. The source code is distributed under
the LGPLv3 Lesser Gnu Public License.

Reference repository: https://codefloe.com/shred/identify

!!! REPOSITORY WAS MOVED FROM CODEBERG TO CODEFLOE !!!

The source code is intentionally not part of this package. If you want
to modify the code, please consider contributing to the reference
repository. This is better than having an unknown number of forks and
different versions of the code floating around.
